WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:05.850
next question that came in, David, for all
of the failed talk about a civil war after

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:12.550
the election results, what could actually
start a second American civil war?

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:16.299
So let's talk about this in a couple of different
ways.

00:00:16.299 --> 00:00:21.220
First of all, a lot of times when people talk
about an American civil war or the division

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:27.359
of the United States into two countries, they
are talking about red states, blue states.

00:00:27.359 --> 00:00:34.470
And the difficulty of that is that the geographical
boundaries of what red state, blue state would

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:43.720
be are relatively loose in the sense that
many red states still have 30, 35, 40, even

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:46.540
45 percent Democratic voters.

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:52.660
Many blue states still have 30, 35, 40, 45
percent Republican voters.

00:00:52.660 --> 00:01:00.829
So this idea, you know, it's not a requirement
for a civil war that the lines be super clear.

00:01:00.829 --> 00:01:07.329
If you look at Italy in the early 40s, you
had this north south thing, but the north

00:01:07.329 --> 00:01:10.409
was filled with those sympathetic to the south
and vice versa.

00:01:10.409 --> 00:01:17.349
You can look at sort of modern civil war,
Syria and Ukraine, they are more really sustained

00:01:17.349 --> 00:01:23.549
sectarian insurgencies than clear civil wars,
the way we had the union in the Confederacy

00:01:23.549 --> 00:01:25.119
in the American Civil War.

00:01:25.119 --> 00:01:30.149
The other really interesting thing to consider
is that just for the sake of a thought experiment,

00:01:30.149 --> 00:01:35.299
if we want to think about a second American
civil war, a long Confederacy Union lines,

00:01:35.299 --> 00:01:40.560
the Confederacy is completely financially
unsustainable.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:43.610
And we've talked about this before in the
United States.

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:49.729
You have all of these federal programs into
which states pay and out of which they receive

00:01:49.729 --> 00:01:50.729
benefits.

00:01:50.729 --> 00:01:52.119
They receive money.

00:01:52.119 --> 00:01:55.969
The blue states dramatically subsidize the
red states.

00:01:55.969 --> 00:02:02.579
And so you have a lot of states in the U.S.,
overwhelmingly red states run by Republicans

00:02:02.579 --> 00:02:08.289
that were it not for being subsidized by money
from blue states, they wouldn't be viable.

00:02:08.289 --> 00:02:14.230
And what you would have if you were to divide
the country in the imaginary second civil

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:22.970
war into factions that sort of line up with
civil war, union and Confederacy.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:29.510
If there were to be a separation, the Confederacy
would be in 2020.

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:34.780
They would be bankrupt very, very quickly
and it would be a desperate situation there.

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:42.900
So it also is, practically speaking, not going
to it doesn't it doesn't make any sense now

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:47.370
in terms of now that we've gotten all of that
out of the way, what could really get the

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:52.569
United States to boil over, maybe not into
what we would call a civil war, but sustained

00:02:52.569 --> 00:02:59.049
and major sort of sectarian violence and and
fighting?

00:02:59.049 --> 00:03:08.530
One of the things that corporations and the
financial sector and others are really effectively

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:16.670
doing in the United States is they have created
a situation where a lot of people are just

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:23.969
kind of happy enough being able to be on the
couch watching football on Sundays and living

00:03:23.969 --> 00:03:25.209
their lives.

00:03:25.209 --> 00:03:26.829
Not that everybody's lives are perfect.

00:03:26.829 --> 00:03:30.670
There's tons of hunger, poverty, everything
in the United States, but there is enough

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:35.989
people due to cheap stuff from China and credit
card debt and all of these instruments that

00:03:35.989 --> 00:03:36.989
are available.

00:03:36.989 --> 00:03:40.950
You've got a lot of people who they're thresholds
for when they're going to go out in the streets

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:43.579
and do anything is really, really high.

00:03:43.579 --> 00:03:46.579
And it creates a natural disincentive for
people to do it.

00:03:46.579 --> 00:03:54.260
At the same time, low wages, the low savings
rate of the United States, the financial instability

00:03:54.260 --> 00:04:00.709
that so many people experience also makes
it tough to go out in the streets because

00:04:00.709 --> 00:04:03.409
you need to buy food the next day for your
family.

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:07.670
And if you miss a day of work and it's unpaid
and you're not going be able to do that, and

00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:13.400
you need to be able to not have your car repossessed
so that you can go and drive and get the food.

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:18.700
The point is, this is a system that perpetuates
itself.

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:25.690
The status quo perpetuates itself by keeping
keeping people sort of just happy enough that

00:04:25.690 --> 00:04:30.280
they would need a really high bar to be met
before they would go out fighting for anything.

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:36.490
And at the same time, you keep them in a precarious
enough position that they can't afford not

00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:38.520
to work for very long.

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:42.669
That is how you preemptively and systemically
suppress an uprising.

00:04:42.669 --> 00:04:46.310
So I don't know what the answer is about what
it would take for something to boil over,

00:04:46.310 --> 00:04:48.490
to be almost like a civil war.

00:04:48.490 --> 00:04:50.289
You also don't need everybody.

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:56.440
You don't need everybody either fat and happy
or in squalor to have enough people to really

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:57.479
cause chaos.

00:04:57.479 --> 00:04:58.759
There's no doubt about.

00:04:58.759 --> 00:05:06.229
That but it is actually difficult to imagine
what would rise to that level, I think that,

00:05:06.229 --> 00:05:09.819
you know, if Donald Trump were to figure out
a way to steal the election, I think you would

00:05:09.819 --> 00:05:15.569
see protests like we have not seen for I don't
want to say how long decades for sure would

00:05:15.569 --> 00:05:17.190
it rise to a civil war?

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:18.190
I don't even know.

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:18.196
I'm curious to hear from you

